  "description": "Pressurised crew cabin design: the habitable pressure vessel, atmosphere system, and crew accommodation layout that sustain astronauts in flight. Covers aluminium-lithium and composite pressure shells, double-walled meteoroid shielding, the 101 kPa / 21% O2 atmosphere loop with CO2 scrubbing and humidity control, seating and restraint for launch and landing loads, and the windows, hatches, and avionics integration.",
